<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Alright then. This article reminds me a lot of <a href="/scp-1352">SCP-1352</a> in that both involve living dust creatures. It wouldn't be too far out of line for the Foundation to look into whether or not the two phenomena are variations of one another, or if SCP-1352 was created by 2583 or visa versa. As such, I am recommending the following edits:</p>
<p>Changing this:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-2583 is a mobile, sentient structure made of dust. Its baseline form masses 1.7 grams and measures 3.7 centimeters in height. Its form is somewhat indistinct due to its composition, but is roughly humanoid, with four strands of dust representing limbs extending from a central strand which terminates in a spheroid made of dust.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>To this:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-2583 is a mobile, sentient structure made of dust. Its baseline form masses 1.7 grams and measures 3.7 centimeters in height. Its form is somewhat indistinct due to its composition, but is roughly humanoid, with four strands of dust representing limbs extending from a central strand which terminates in a spheroid made of dust.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-263012-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-263012-1')">1</a></sup></p>
</blockquote>
<p>If anyone has other/better examples that could be used here please leave a comment saying so!</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="footnotes-footer">
<div class="title">Footnotes</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-263012-1"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-263012-1')">1</a>. Similarity between SCP-2583 and <a href="/scp-1352">SCP-1352</a> has been noted. Investigation into whether the two phenomena are variations of the same effect, or if one propagated the other, is ongoing.</div>
</div>

